# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every platform, which is
# how the repository already stores them. Without this, git's default on Windows
# rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, and that changes behaviour, not just
# appearance: prompt templates and recorded agent streams are compiled into the
# binary with include_str!, shell completions are compared byte for byte with
# what clap generates, and install.sh stops running under sh.
* text=auto eol=lf
